<title>USA: Sportmart Inc Q1 May 4 loss.</title>
<headline>Sportmart Inc Q1 May 4 loss.</headline>
<dateline>WHEELING, Ill. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>May 4,     Apr 28,</p>
<p>						   1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net sales				 $ 103,932  $ 116,209</p>
<p>Cost of sales, including buying,</p>
<p> distribution and occupancy	     81,311     90,590</p>
<p>Operating Expenses:</p>
<p> Store expenses			     17,506     20,270</p>
<p> General and administrative expenses   4,709	4,634</p>
<p> Store pre-opening expenses		    0	  117</p>
<p>    Operating income			   406	  598</p>
<p> Interest, net			     (1,863)    (1,966)</p>
<p> Other expense				  (18)	(152)</p>
<p> Loss from operations		    (1,475)    (1,520)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit			  (590)	(643)</p>
<p>   Net loss				    (885)	(877)</p>
<p> Net loss per share			 (0.07)     (0.07)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>    common shares outstanding     12,848,265 12,800,028</p>
<p>NOTE: Lower 1997 Q1 sales reflect company's decision to exit the Canadian market at the end of fiscal 1996.</p>
<p>1997 Q1 same store sales fell three percent from the comparable period a year ago.</p>
<p>			 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
